# One row per layer pair a filing holds that another document observed moving together. The
# coupling is filed somewhere else; both of its ends are layers of this filing; and so this
# filing's remainders are not the independent quantizations its own arithmetic takes them for.
#
# Unintended, so both unbalanced and unsettled
#   A spillover is unintended, and that is why it is neither unbalanced nor unsettled but both. The
#   layer at the far end is perfectly deliberate in its own filing. What nobody meant is the reach
#   into your remainder, so neither set of books carries it, and neither filer has anything to
#   answer for. `merge-group-composition` watched delivery headcount move the shift line;
#   `merge-us-member` holds both layers and has not looked.
#
# A referral, never a violation
#   A filing is not the system, and a second document's observation is a projection onto this one
#   rather than an accusation against it. Nobody here filed anything wrong: `enterprise-contract`
#   states its coupling search as `unmeasured` and its note says in prose exactly what this
#   relation says in rows: "the same two layers are the subject of refutation.xml ... so this is
#   the honest prior state rather than a claim of independence". The author knew.
#
# The far filing is named; the bound is not copied
#   merge-holding-composition argues at length that a coupling carried up a level cannot survive at
#   full strength and had to be re-observed. A number copied across a boundary is a number nobody
#   took.
-- pm:couplings/pm:coupling, projected onto every other filing holding both of its ends.
SELECT c.filing        AS observed_in,
       b.filing        AS borne_by,
       c.from_layer,
       c.to_layer,
       c.mode          AS observed_mode,
       c.unit          AS observed_unit,
       s.answer        AS their_search,
       sc.extent       AS their_extent
FROM      (
    :compose(entries/couplings.sqlc)
) c
JOIN      (
    :compose(layers/every_layer.sqlc)
) b  ON b.layer = c.from_layer AND b.filing <> c.filing
JOIN      (
    :compose(layers/every_layer.sqlc)
) b2 ON b2.filing = b.filing AND b2.layer = c.to_layer
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(epistemics/coupling_searches.sqlc)
) s  ON s.filing = b.filing
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(epistemics/scopes.sqlc)
) sc ON sc.filing = b.filing
